   ('28-each-brotherly-compassion-that-man-hath-on-his-fellow-chr', 'XXVIII', 'Each brotherly compassion that man hath on his fellow Christians, with charity, it is Christ in him', ('CHAPTER XXVIII', '"Each brotherly compassion that man hath on his fellow Christians, with\n                     charity, it is Christ in him"'), 'Thus I saw how Christ hath compassion on us', '[2] "gruching."'),
   ('29-how-could-all-be-well-for-the-great-harm-that-is-come-by', 'XXIX', 'How could all be well, for the great harm that is come by sin to the creature?', ('CHAPTER XXIX', '"How could all be well, for the great harm that is come by sin to the\n                              creature?"'), 'But in this I stood beholding things general, troublously', '[2] "asyeth making". See preceding note.'),
   ('30-two-parts-of-truth-the-part-that-is-open-our-saviour-and', 'XXX', 'Two parts of Truth: the part that is open: our Saviour and our salvation; and the part that is hid and shut up from us: all beside our salvation', ('CHAPTER XXX', '"Two parts of Truth: the part that is open: our Saviour and our\n salvation;--and the part that is hid and shut up from us: all beside\n                            our salvation"'), 'He gave me understanding of two parts [of truth].', 'not to wel wetyn his counselye."'),
